# title: Barrier reverse convertible
# category: Structured notes
# underlyings: 1
# source: Rubinstein & Reiner, Breaking Down the Barriers, Risk, 1991
# source: Bouzoubaa & Osseiran, Exotic Options and Hybrids: A Guide to Structuring, Pricing and Trading, Wiley, 2010
# summary: Quarterly 2.5% coupons; the capital is at risk only if the stock ever closes at or below 60% of its initial level and ends below it.
#
# Notional 1000. Coupons are paid whatever happens. Knock-in barrier 60%,
# daily closes; if it was touched and the stock ends below its initial
# level, the capital is repaid in proportion to the fall.

2027-01-04
    s0 = spot()
    ki = 0

schedule(2027-01-05, 2027-12-30, 1D, US, F)
    if spot() <= 0.60 * s0 then ki = 1 endIf

2027-04-05  2027-07-06  2027-10-04
    pays 1000 * 0.025

2028-01-04
    if spot() <= 0.60 * s0 then ki = 1 endIf
    pays 1000 * 0.025
    if ki = 1 and spot() < s0 then pays 1000 * spot() / s0 else pays 1000 endIf
